{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `deaths_obs`, a deterministic flattened copy of the `deaths[EpidemicStart[m]:N[m], m]` entries scored in the original model.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the looped slice likelihood with one top-level protected sampling statement, `deaths_obs ~ neg_binomial_2(E_deaths_obs, phi)`, using context index arrays to gather the matching expected-death means. Vectorized the elementwise prior loop for `y[m]` to `y ~ exponential(1 / tau)` so the parameter is scored once outside loops. The original `deaths` array is not declared in the SafeStan model; its modelled entries are supplied through the protected flattened copy.

Data relation: `N_deaths_obs`, `deaths_obs`, `deaths_obs_day`, and `deaths_obs_country` are deterministically constructed by scanning countries `m` and available days `i` with `EpidemicStart[m] <= i <= N[m]` and `1 <= i <= N2`, then copying `deaths[i, m]`. For the supplied synthetic data this set is empty, so the added arrays are empty.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> M; // number of countries
  int<lower=1> P; // number of covariates
  int<lower=1> N0; // number of days for which to impute infections
  array[M] int<lower=1> N; // days of observed data for country m. each entry must be <= N2
  int<lower=1> N2; // days of observed data + // of days to forecast
  array[N2, M] int cases; // reported cases
  matrix[N2, M] f; // h * s
  array[M] matrix[N2, P] X; // features matrix
  array[M] int EpidemicStart;
  array[M] real pop;
  array[N2] real SI; // fixed pre-calculated SI using emprical data from Neil
  int<lower=0> N_deaths_obs; // number of reported-death entries scored by the likelihood
  array[N_deaths_obs] int<lower=0> deaths_obs; // flattened reported deaths
  array[N_deaths_obs] int<lower=1, upper=N2> deaths_obs_day;
  array[N_deaths_obs] int<lower=1, upper=M> deaths_obs_country;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N2] SI_rev; // SI in reverse order
  array[M] vector[N2] f_rev; // f in reversed order

  for (i in 1 : N2) {
    SI_rev[i] = SI[N2 - i + 1];
  }

  for (m in 1 : M) {
    for (i in 1 : N2) {
      f_rev[m, i] = f[N2 - i + 1, m];
    }
  }
}
parameters {
  array[M] real<lower=0> mu; // intercept for Rt
  array[P] real<lower=0> alpha_hier; // sudo parameter for the hier term for alpha
  real<lower=0> gamma;
  vector[M] lockdown;
  real<lower=0> kappa;
  array[M] real<lower=0> y;
  real<lower=0> phi;
  real<lower=0> tau;
  array[M] real<lower=0> ifr_noise;
}
transformed parameters {
  vector[P] alpha;
  matrix[N2, M] prediction = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
  matrix[N2, M] E_deaths = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
  matrix[N2, M] Rt = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
  matrix[N2, M] Rt_adj = Rt;
  vector[N_deaths_obs] E_deaths_obs = rep_vector(0, N_deaths_obs);

  {
    matrix[N2, M] cumm_sum = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
    for (i in 1 : P) {
      alpha[i] = alpha_hier[i] - (log(1.05) / 6.0);
    }
    for (m in 1 : M) {
      prediction[1 : N0, m] = rep_vector(y[m], N0); // learn the number of cases in the first N0 days
      cumm_sum[2 : N0, m] = cumulative_sum(prediction[2 : N0, m]);

      Rt[ : , m] = mu[m] * exp(-X[m] * alpha - X[m][ : , 5] * lockdown[m]);
      Rt_adj[1 : N0, m] = Rt[1 : N0, m];
      for (i in (N0 + 1) : N2) {
        real convolution = dot_product(sub_col(prediction, 1, m, i - 1),
                                       tail(SI_rev, i - 1));
        cumm_sum[i, m] = cumm_sum[i - 1, m] + prediction[i - 1, m];
        Rt_adj[i, m] = ((pop[m] - cumm_sum[i, m]) / pop[m]) * Rt[i, m];
        prediction[i, m] = Rt_adj[i, m] * convolution;
      }
      E_deaths[1, m] = 1e-15 * prediction[1, m];
      for (i in 2 : N2) {
        E_deaths[i, m] = ifr_noise[m]
                         * dot_product(sub_col(prediction, 1, m, i - 1),
                                       tail(f_rev[m], i - 1));
      }
    }
  }
  if (N_deaths_obs > 0) {
    for (j in 1 : N_deaths_obs) {
      E_deaths_obs[j] = E_deaths[deaths_obs_day[j], deaths_obs_country[j]];
    }
  }
}
model {
  tau ~ exponential(0.03);
  y ~ exponential(1 / tau);
  gamma ~ normal(0, .2);
  lockdown ~ normal(0, gamma);
  phi ~ normal(0, 5);
  kappa ~ normal(0, 0.5);
  mu ~ normal(3.28, kappa); // citation: https://academic.oup.com/jtm/article/27/2/taaa021/5735319
  alpha_hier ~ gamma(.1667, 1);
  ifr_noise ~ normal(1, 0.1);
  deaths_obs ~ neg_binomial_2(E_deaths_obs, phi);
}
generated quantities {
  matrix[N2, M] prediction0 = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
  matrix[N2, M] E_deaths0 = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);

  {
    matrix[N2, M] cumm_sum0 = rep_matrix(0, N2, M);
    for (m in 1 : M) {
      for (i in 2 : N0) {
        cumm_sum0[i, m] = cumm_sum0[i - 1, m] + y[m];
      }
      prediction0[1 : N0, m] = rep_vector(y[m], N0);
      for (i in (N0 + 1) : N2) {
        real convolution0 = dot_product(sub_col(prediction0, 1, m, i - 1),
                                        tail(SI_rev, i - 1));
        cumm_sum0[i, m] = cumm_sum0[i - 1, m] + prediction0[i - 1, m];
        prediction0[i, m] = ((pop[m] - cumm_sum0[i, m]) / pop[m]) * mu[m]
                            * convolution0;
      }
      E_deaths0[1, m] = 1e-15 * prediction0[1, m];
      for (i in 2 : N2) {
        E_deaths0[i, m] = ifr_noise[m]
                          * dot_product(sub_col(prediction0, 1, m, i - 1),
                                        tail(f_rev[m], i - 1));
      }
    }
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"EpidemicStart":[2,4,6,5],"M":4,"N":[5,2,3,1],"N0":2,"N2":1,"P":3,"SI":[3.9517523740994944],"X":[[[5.333894583435004,2.318217577951397,4.5172449971674284]],[[4.752997699315685,2.5471228262086525,2.5887143707352585]],[[4.510329601923708,2.8546229782661885,3.2303119450901563]],[[3.2855403275246937,6.5650323002690385,6.624519737373351]]],"cases":[[3,2,6,6]],"f":[[4.713860668985641,6.800386115138112,5.862074831726254,3.3371807005911287]],"pop":[6.441116999327836,2.632601711698888,3.529238534548089,5.378920367694228],"N_deaths_obs":0,"deaths_obs":[],"deaths_obs_day":[],"deaths_obs_country":[]}","protected_variables":["deaths_obs"]}
